{"name":"Angry Gargoyle","hex":"#9799a6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Displaying or feeling anger.","Inflamed and painful."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An angry person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angry"},{"term":"gargoyle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A carved grotesque figure on a spout which conveys water away from the gutters.","Any decorative carved grotesque figure on a building."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gargoyle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anger","blocks":[{"text":"Anger, also known as wrath or rage, is an intense emotional state involving a strong, uncomfortable and non-cooperative response to a perceived provocation, hurt, or threat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Le_Col%C3%A8re_m%C3%AAl%C3%A9e_de_crainte_%28from_Caract%C3%A8res_des_passions%2C_grav%C3%A9s_sur_les_desseins_de_l%27illustre_Monsieur_le_Brun%29_MET_DP854052.jpg/330px-Le_Col%C3%A8re_m%C3%AAl%C3%A9e_de_crainte_%28from_Caract%C3%A8res_des_passions%2C_grav%C3%A9s_sur_les_desseins_de_l%27illustre_Monsieur_le_Brun%29_MET_DP854052.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anger"},{"title":"Gargoyle","blocks":[{"text":"In architecture, and specifically Gothic architecture, a gargoyle is a carved or formed grotesque with a spout designed to convey water from a roof and away from the side of a building, thereby preventing it from running down masonry walls and eroding the mortar between. Architects often used multiple gargoyles on a building to divide the flow of rainwater off the roof to minimize potential damage from rainstorms. A trough is cut in the back of the gargoyle and rainwater typically exits through the open mouth. Gargoyles are usually elongated fantastical animals because their length determines how far water is directed from the wall. When Gothic flying buttresses were used, aqueducts were sometimes cut into the buttress to divert water over the aisle walls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Notre-Dame_Rzygacze.JPG/330px-Notre-Dame_Rzygacze.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_Rage_of_Achilles_by_Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo.jpeg/500px-The_Rage_of_Achilles_by_Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_Rage_of_Achilles_by_Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo.jpeg/500px-The_Rage_of_Achilles_by_Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Anger of Achilles, by Giovanni Battista Tiepolo depicts the Greek hero attacking Agamemnon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Rage_of_Achilles_by_Giovanni_Battista_Tiepolo.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/SERGI01rob-2.jpg/500px-SERGI01rob-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/SERGI01rob-2.jpg/500px-SERGI01rob-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A visibly angered Washington Luís, President of Brazil (back seat) leaving the Guanabara Palace after his overthrow during the Revolution of 1930 (October 24)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASERGI01rob-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Nevrovitamine_4_P-FG-ES-01835.jpg/500px-Nevrovitamine_4_P-FG-ES-01835.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Nevrovitamine_4_P-FG-ES-01835.jpg/1280px-Nevro